  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increasing access to lifesaving health services for Haitians affected by insecurity caused by gang violence.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to maintain and increase access to lifesaving health services for the population of the ZMPP areas, affected by insecurity and gang violence, including pregnant women and people living in IDP sites. The WHO project provides early warning and rapid response mechanisms to epidemics, timely obstetric emergency care and surgical health services. The intervention provides humanitarian assistance to 78,870 people (25,883 men, 28,615 women and 24,372 children), including 3,155 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
